---
import GameShell from '../layouts/GameShell.astro'
import { PATTERNS } from '../lib/dark-patterns'
import { withBase } from '../lib/base'

/**
 * Dark Patterns — eleven manipulative UI tricks, reproduced as working fake
 * websites rather than described in a bullet list.
 *
 * Every one of these is a documented pattern, not an invented vibe — see
 * src/lib/dark-patterns.ts for the citation attached to each — and every
 * fake site is its own small, convincing lie: its own name, its own brand
 * colour, its own voice, so this reads as eleven places rather than one
 * template with the copy swapped. The one thing they all share on purpose is
 * the visual grammar: the trick is always the site's loudest pill; the honest
 * way through is always the small, quiet line of text. That contrast is the
 * actual lesson, and eleven repetitions of it are what make it recognisable
 * afterwards, on a real site, without this page open next to it.
 *
 * The pattern's name is not shown until you have acted. The old page printed
 * "Confirmshaming" above the confirmshaming widget, which is a spoiler for
 * the only thing the widget is testing.
 *
 * In the shell: Score is how many you dodged, Site is progress through the
 * eleven, Moves are the ones you fell for, Best is your best run.
 *
 * Nothing here is graded on cleverness. `resolve('dodged' | 'fell', note)` is
 * the whole verdict, and it is never hidden behind a puzzle — every pattern
 * can be beaten the first time by anyone who happens to look closely, the
 * same way the real ones can.
 */
const total = PATTERNS.length
---

<GameShell
  slug="dark-patterns"
  labels={{ score: 'Dodged', best: 'Best run', level: 'Site', moves: 'Fell for' }}
  initial={{ score: '0', level: `0 / ${total}`, moves: '0' }}
>
  <div class="dp-intro" id="intro">
    <p class="label meta">Eleven websites · one lesson</p>
    <h2 class="dp-intro-title">Every one of these sites wants <em class="wonk">something</em> from you.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Each is built around a trick the people who study this for a living have
      catalogued and named. Do the ordinary errand each site gives you. Look
      closely. Some are genuinely hard to beat.
    </p>
    <button type="button" class="pill pill--hero" id="begin">
      <span>Open the first site</span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </button>
    <ul class="dp-domains" aria-label="The eleven sites">
      {PATTERNS.map((p) => <li class="tag">{p.site}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="dp-play" id="play" hidden>
    <div class="dp-window" id="window" data-brand="lilac">
      <div class="dp-chrome">
        <span class="dp-lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="dp-addr">
          <i class="dp-favicon" id="favicon" aria-hidden="true">F</i>
          <span class="dp-url" id="url">example.com</span>
        </span>
      </div>
      <i class="dp-load" id="load" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <div class="dp-site" id="site" tabindex="-1" aria-label="The website">
        <div class="dp-brandbar">
          <p class="dp-wordmark" id="wordmark">Site</p>
          <span class="dp-nav" aria-hidden="true"><span>Shop</span><span>About</span><span>Help</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-body" id="slot"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="dp-notes">
      <div class="dp-brief">
        <p class="label meta" id="siteNo">Site 1 of {total}</p>
        <p class="label dp-errand-lbl">Your errand</p>
        <p class="dp-errand" id="lede">—</p>
        <ol class="dp-tally" id="tally" aria-label="Your record so far">
          {PATTERNS.map(() => <li><span class="sr-only">Not yet</span></li>)}
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-verdict" id="verdict" hidden tabindex="-1">
        <p class="label dp-v-head"><span class="dp-v-sign" id="vSign" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span id="vHead">You spotted it</span></p>
        <h3 class="dp-v-title" id="vTitle">Pattern</h3>
        <p class="dp-v-note" id="vNote"></p>
        <p class="dp-v-reveal" id="vReveal"></p>
        <p class="dp-v-cite" id="vCite"></p>
        <button type="button" class="pill pill--ink" id="next">
          <span id="nextLbl">Next site</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </button>
        <p class="dp-keys"><kbd>N</kbd> or <kbd>Enter</kbd></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="howto">
    <p>
      Eleven fake websites, one at a time. Each gives you an ordinary errand —
      buy a thing, cancel a thing, change a setting. Each is built around a
      real, catalogued manipulation.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>The trick is always the loudest button.</b> The honest way through is usually small, plain text.</li>
      <li>Read every sentence twice, especially checkboxes. Sometimes the right answer is to wait.</li>
      <li>After each site you will see what the trick was called and who named it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Dodge as many as you can. Your best is your highest number dodged.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <details class="dp-real" slot="after">
    <summary class="label">Where these come from</summary>
    <p>
      Nothing here is randomised against you and nothing is a puzzle with a
      trick answer — every pattern can be beaten the first time by looking
      closely at the same two things every time: which option is loud and
      which one is quiet, and what a sentence actually says once you read it
      twice. That is also exactly how the real ones work.
    </p>
    <p>
      The names are not this site's invention. Most come from Harry
      Brignull's original 2010 list — he coined the term "dark pattern"
      cataloguing exactly these — and the newer ones from a 2019 Princeton/CHI
      study that scraped eleven thousand shopping sites looking for them, or
      the FTC's 2022 report to Congress on the same subject.
    </p>
    <p>Related: <a href={withBase('/not-a-robot/')}>I'm Not a Robot</a> is the other page here built out of real interface conventions rather than a metaphor for them.</p>
  </details>
</GameShell>

<script type="application/json" id="game-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(PATTERNS)} />

<script>
  import { createShell } from '../lib/game-shell'
  import { sfx, unlock } from '../lib/audio'
  import { recordPlay } from '../lib/stats'
  import { dailyFor, dailyTarget } from '../data/game-meta'

  type Pattern = { id: string; title: string; site: string; real: string; lede: string; reveal: string }
  const PATTERNS = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('game-data')!.textContent!) as Pattern[]
  const TOTAL = PATTERNS.length

  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!
  const intro = $('intro'), play = $('play')
  const win = $('window'), site = $('site'), slot = $('slot')
  const verdict = $('verdict')
  const tally = [...$('tally').children] as HTMLLIElement[]

  /**
   * Each fake site's brand. One block colour each (the system has five and
   * ink, so some repeat — the voice of the wordmark is what keeps two sky
   * sites apart), and the trap button always wears it.
   */
  type Brand = { name: string; block: 'cobalt' | 'mint' | 'sky' | 'red' | 'lilac' | 'ink'; voice: 'serif' | 'sans' | 'shout' | 'lower' }
  const BRANDS: Record<string, Brand> = {
    basket: { name: 'Fenwick & Oates', block: 'lilac', voice: 'serif' },
    confirmshame: { name: 'The Daily Brew', block: 'mint', voice: 'serif' },
    roach: { name: 'Chorus+', block: 'red', voice: 'sans' },
    urgency: { name: 'GET IT NOW', block: 'cobalt', voice: 'shout' },
    ads: { name: 'Freeware Depot', block: 'sky', voice: 'sans' },
    drip: { name: 'ticketloop', block: 'mint', voice: 'lower' },
    continuity: { name: 'Loomline', block: 'sky', voice: 'serif' },
    trick: { name: 'Account settings', block: 'ink', voice: 'sans' },
    zuckering: { name: 'frennet', block: 'sky', voice: 'lower' },
    social: { name: 'NIMBUS', block: 'cobalt', voice: 'shout' },
    nagging: { name: 'The Daily Briefing', block: 'red', voice: 'serif' },
  }

  type Outcome = 'dodged' | 'fell'
  type Api = {
    resolve: (outcome: Outcome, note: string) => void
    /** An interval that stops while the game is paused and dies with the site. */
    every: (fn: () => void, ms: number) => void
    /** A small knock — a new wall arriving, not a wrong answer. */
    knock: () => void
  }
  type Mount = (host: HTMLElement, api: Api) => void
  type Result = { id: string; title: string; real: string; outcome: Outcome; note: string }

  let results: Result[] = []
  let idx = -1
  let resolved = false
  let timers: number[] = []
  const clearTimers = () => { timers.forEach(clearInterval); timers = [] }

  const shell = createShell({ slug: 'dark-patterns', onRestart: restart })

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* The eleven sites                                                        */
  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  const on = (host: HTMLElement, sel: string, fn: (e: Event) => void) =>
    host.querySelector(sel)!.addEventListener('click', fn)

  const MOUNTS: Record<string, Mount> = {
    basket(host, api) {
      const items = [['Wool scarf', 28], ['Reading lamp', 44], ['Ceramic mug', 14]] as const
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">New this week</p>
        <h3 class="dp-h">Three things, made well.</h3>
        <div class="dp-products">
          ${items.map(([name, price]) => `
            <div class="dp-product">
              <b>${name}</b><span class="dp-price">$${price}</span>
              <button type="button" class="dp-trap dp-buy" data-item="${name}" data-price="${price}">Add to basket</button>
            </div>`).join('')}
        </div>`
      host.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.dp-buy').forEach((btn) =>
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          sfx.tick()
          const item = btn.dataset.item!
          const price = Number(btn.dataset.price)
          host.innerHTML = `
            <h3 class="dp-h">Your basket</h3>
            <label class="dp-line"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled><span>${item}</span><b>$${price.toFixed(2)}</b></label>
            <label class="dp-line"><input type="checkbox" checked class="extra" data-p="4.99"><span>Extended protection plan</span><b>$4.99</b></label>
            <label class="dp-line"><input type="checkbox" checked class="extra" data-p="2.99"><span>Fenwick Rewards membership</span><b>$2.99</b></label>
            <p class="dp-total"><span>Total</span><b id="total"></b></p>
            <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="checkout">Complete purchase</button>`
          api.knock()
          const paint = () => {
            const extra = [...host.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('.extra:checked')].reduce((n, x) => n + Number(x.dataset.p), 0)
            host.querySelector('#total')!.textContent = `$${(price + extra).toFixed(2)}`
          }
          host.querySelectorAll('.extra').forEach((x) => x.addEventListener('change', paint))
          paint()
          on(host, '#checkout', () => {
            const extras = host.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('.extra:checked').length
            if (extras === 0) api.resolve('dodged', 'You unchecked both extras before paying for anything you never chose.')
            else api.resolve('fell', `You paid for ${extras} thing${extras > 1 ? 's' : ''} that rode along with your actual order.`)
          })
        }),
      )
    },

    confirmshame(host, api) {
      host.innerHTML = `
        <div class="dp-behind" aria-hidden="true">
          <p class="dp-h">Why your morning coffee tastes flat</p>
          <i></i><i></i><i class="short"></i><i></i><i class="short"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-modal" role="dialog" aria-label="Newsletter">
          <p class="dp-kicker">Before you go</p>
          <p class="dp-modal-q">Join the Brew Circle for 15% off your next bag?</p>
          <div class="dp-acts">
            <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="yes">Yes, sign me up</button>
            <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="no">No thanks, I like paying full price</button>
          </div>
        </div>`
      on(host, '#yes', () => api.resolve('fell', 'You signed up rather than click a sentence written to make declining feel foolish.'))
      on(host, '#no', () => api.resolve('dodged', 'You clicked past the guilt trip without it changing your answer.'))
    },

    roach(host, api) {
      const step0 = () => {
        host.innerHTML = `
          <h3 class="dp-h">Manage your plan</h3>
          <p class="dp-line is-plain"><span>Chorus+ Premium</span><b>$17.99 / month</b></p>
          <p class="dp-small">Renews on the 3rd. You can cancel at any time.</p>
          <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="cancel">Cancel subscription</button>`
        on(host, '#cancel', () => { sfx.click(); step1() })
      }
      const wall = (text: string, trap: string, honest: string, onTrap: () => void, onHonest: () => void) => {
        api.knock()
        host.innerHTML = `
          <div class="dp-stall">
            <p class="dp-kicker">Wait —</p>
            <p class="dp-modal-q">${text}</p>
            <div class="dp-acts">
              ${trap ? `<button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="trap">${trap}</button>` : ''}
              <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="honest">${honest}</button>
            </div>
          </div>`
        if (trap) on(host, '#trap', onTrap)
        on(host, '#honest', onHonest)
      }
      const step1 = () => wall(
        'Before you go, here is 50% off for the next three months.', 'Keep my discount', 'No, cancel anyway',
        () => api.resolve('fell', 'The first retention offer was enough to keep the subscription running.'),
        () => { sfx.tick(); step2() })
      const step2 = () => wall(
        'You will lose offline downloads, 4K streaming, and a watchlist of 214 titles.', 'Stay subscribed', 'Continue cancelling',
        () => api.resolve('fell', 'The list of what you would lose was the second wall, and it worked.'),
        () => { sfx.tick(); step3() })
      const step3 = () => wall(
        'Final step: call 1-800-555-0199, Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm, to complete your cancellation.', '', '…that is the final step?',
        () => {},
        () => api.resolve('dodged', 'You made it through every wall, including the one that demands a phone call during business hours.'))
      step0()
    },

    urgency(host, api) {
      let remaining = 12
      let resets = 0
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">Flash sale · noise-cancelling headphones</p>
        <p class="dp-deal"><s>$249</s> <b>$99</b></p>
        <p class="dp-clock-line">Sale ends in <b class="dp-clock" id="clock">00:12</b></p>
        <div class="dp-acts is-stacked">
          <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="buy">Buy now before it ends</button>
          <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="watch">Just watch the clock</button>
        </div>
        <p class="dp-small" id="note" aria-live="polite"></p>`
      const clock = host.querySelector('#clock') as HTMLElement
      const note = host.querySelector('#note')!
      api.every(() => {
        remaining--
        if (remaining < 0) {
          remaining = 12
          resets++
          clock.classList.add('is-reset')
          setTimeout(() => clock.classList.remove('is-reset'), 260)
        }
        clock.textContent = `00:${String(remaining).padStart(2, '0')}`
      }, 260)
      on(host, '#buy', () => {
        if (resets > 0) api.resolve('dodged', `You waited long enough to see the clock reset ${resets} time${resets > 1 ? 's' : ''} before buying anything.`)
        else api.resolve('fell', 'You bought before the clock ever finished a single lap — the exact window this pattern is built for.')
      })
      on(host, '#watch', () => {
        if (resets > 0) api.resolve('dodged', `You watched it reset ${resets} time${resets > 1 ? 's' : ''} instead of buying under the clock.`)
        else { sfx.tick(); note.textContent = 'Keep watching…' }
      })
    },

    ads(host, api) {
      const decoys = [['DirectDownload Pro', 'cobalt'], ['FastGet Installer', 'lilac'], ['SafeFile Setup', 'sky']] as const
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">PhotoTrim 4 · free · 2.1 MB</p>
        <h3 class="dp-h">Download PhotoTrim 4</h3>
        <div class="dp-dlgrid">
          ${decoys.map(([d, c]) => `<button type="button" class="dp-trap dp-decoy" data-c="${c}"><span>${d}</span><small>Advertisement</small></button>`).join('')}
          <button type="button" class="dp-real-dl" id="real"><span>Download</span><small>PhotoTrim 4 · 2.1 MB</small></button>
        </div>`
      host.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.dp-decoy').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => api.resolve('fell', 'That button was an advertisement styled to match the download you actually came for.')))
      on(host, '#real', () => api.resolve('dodged', 'You found the real, plainest button on the page, sitting last and smallest.'))
    },

    drip(host, api) {
      let peeked = false
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">Friday · doors 7pm</p>
        <h3 class="dp-h">The Weather Station, live</h3>
        <p class="dp-line is-plain"><span>General admission</span><b class="dp-big">$45.00</b></p>
        <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="continue">Continue</button>`
      on(host, '#continue', () => {
        sfx.tick()
        api.knock()
        host.innerHTML = `
          <h3 class="dp-h">Order review</h3>
          <p class="dp-row"><span>Ticket</span><b>$45.00</b></p>
          <p class="dp-row"><span>Service fee</span><b>$9.50</b></p>
          <p class="dp-row"><span>Facility fee</span><b>$6.00</b></p>
          <p class="dp-row"><span>Order processing fee</span><b>$3.25</b></p>
          <p class="dp-total"><span>Total</span><b>$63.75</b></p>
          <div class="dp-acts">
            <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="confirm">Confirm $63.75</button>
            <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="peek">Wait, let me check that</button>
          </div>`
        on(host, '#peek', (e) => {
          peeked = true
          sfx.tick()
          ;(e.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement).textContent = 'That is 42% more than the price you compared.'
        })
        on(host, '#confirm', () => {
          if (peeked) api.resolve('dodged', 'You stopped to add up the fees before confirming anything.')
          else api.resolve('fell', 'You confirmed a total 42% above the price you started with, without adding it up first.')
        })
      })
    },

    continuity(host, api) {
      let expanded = false
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">Loomline Pro · 14 days free</p>
        <h3 class="dp-h">Start your free trial</h3>
        <label class="dp-field"><span class="sr-only">Card number (this is a fake site: type anything or nothing)</span>
          <input type="text" placeholder="Card number" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off"></label>
        <button type="button" class="dp-honest dp-fine" id="fine">+ after your trial ends…</button>
        <label class="dp-line"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled><span>I agree to the trial terms</span></label>
        <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="start">Start free trial</button>`
      on(host, '#fine', (e) => {
        expanded = true
        sfx.tick()
        ;(e.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement).textContent = '$89.99 a month, automatically, unless cancelled first.'
      })
      on(host, '#start', () => {
        if (expanded) api.resolve('dodged', 'You opened the fine print before handing over a card number.')
        else api.resolve('fell', 'You started the trial without reading what it quietly turns into.')
      })
    },

    trick(host, api) {
      host.innerHTML = `
        <h3 class="dp-h">Privacy</h3>
        <p class="dp-small">Update your preferences, then save.</p>
        <label class="dp-line"><input type="checkbox" id="a" checked><span>Don't disable anonymous usage tracking</span></label>
        <label class="dp-line"><input type="checkbox" id="b"><span>Send me occasional product emails</span></label>
        <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="save">Save settings</button>`
      on(host, '#save', () => {
        const stillOn = (host.querySelector('#a') as HTMLInputElement).checked
        if (!stillOn) api.resolve('dodged', 'Unchecking "don’t disable" is what actually disables it, and you worked that out.')
        else api.resolve('fell', 'The box stayed checked — read literally, "don’t disable" checked means tracking stayed on.')
      })
    },

    zuckering(host, api) {
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">Welcome to frennet</p>
        <h3 class="dp-h">Choose your privacy</h3>
        <button type="button" class="dp-trap is-big" id="shareall">Share everything (recommended)</button>
        <p class="dp-center"><button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="custom">Customise individual settings</button></p>`
      on(host, '#shareall', () => { sfx.tick(); confirmA() })
      on(host, '#custom', () => api.resolve('dodged', 'You went straight past the big button to the grey link that actually does what you want.'))
      function confirmA() {
        api.knock()
        host.innerHTML = `
          <h3 class="dp-h">Also share your contacts, so we can find your friends?</h3>
          <div class="dp-acts">
            <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="y1">Yes, share contacts</button>
            <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="n1">Ask me later</button>
          </div>`
        on(host, '#y1', () => { sfx.tick(); confirmB() })
        on(host, '#n1', () => api.resolve('fell', 'You still ended up on "Share everything" — declining one follow-up does not undo the button already pressed.'))
      }
      function confirmB() {
        api.knock()
        host.innerHTML = `
          <h3 class="dp-h">Last thing — share your activity with advertising partners too?</h3>
          <div class="dp-acts">
            <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="y2">Yes, share activity</button>
            <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="n2">Ask me later</button>
          </div>`
        for (const id of ['#y2', '#n2'])
          on(host, id, () => api.resolve('fell', 'Every path out of "Share everything" turned out to be another version of yes.'))
      }
    },

    social(host, api) {
      const names = ['Jordan in Austin', 'Casey in Denver', 'Morgan in Miami']
      let count = 0
      host.innerHTML = `
        <p class="dp-kicker">Only 3 left</p>
        <h3 class="dp-h">The Weekender duffel</h3>
        <p class="dp-line is-plain"><span>Waxed canvas, brass fittings</span><b class="dp-big">$68</b></p>
        <div class="dp-acts is-stacked">
          <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="buy">Buy now — almost gone</button>
          <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="watch">Just watch the corner for a bit</button>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-toasts" aria-live="polite"></div>`
      const layer = host.querySelector('.dp-toasts')!
      on(host, '#watch', (e) => {
        const btn = e.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement
        btn.disabled = true
        btn.textContent = 'Watching…'
        api.every(() => {
          count++
          const el = document.createElement('p')
          el.className = 'dp-toast'
          el.textContent = `${names[count % names.length]} just bought this · 2 minutes ago`
          layer.prepend(el)
          while (layer.children.length > 2) layer.lastElementChild!.remove()
          sfx.tick()
          if (count >= 6)
            api.resolve('dodged', `You watched ${count} of them cycle through the same three names and the same three cities, always "2 minutes ago".`)
        }, 650)
      })
      on(host, '#buy', () => api.resolve('fell', 'You bought under the pressure of activity that was never real.'))
    },

    nagging(host, api) {
      let asks = 0
      const MAX = 3
      const prompt = (last: boolean) => `
        <div class="dp-behind" aria-hidden="true">
          <p class="dp-h">Markets open higher as rates hold</p>
          <i></i><i class="short"></i><i></i><i></i><i class="short"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-prompt" role="dialog" aria-label="Notification request">
          <p><b>dailybriefing.news</b> wants to</p>
          <p class="dp-small">Show notifications${asks > 1 ? ` · asked ${asks} times` : ''}</p>
          <div class="dp-acts">
            <button type="button" class="dp-trap" id="allow">Allow</button>
            <button type="button" class="dp-honest" id="not">${last ? 'Never ask again' : 'Not now'}</button>
          </div>
        </div>`
      const render = () => {
        asks++
        const last = asks > MAX
        host.innerHTML = prompt(last)
        if (asks > 1) api.knock()
        on(host, '#allow', () => api.resolve('fell', last
          ? `You said no ${MAX} times, and said yes the moment it finally offered to stop asking.`
          : `You gave in on ask number ${asks}.`))
        on(host, '#not', () => {
          if (last) api.resolve('dodged', `You said no ${MAX + 1} times in a row rather than give in.`)
          else { sfx.tick(); setTimeout(render, 480) }
        })
      }
      render()
    },
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Runner                                                                  */
  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  const dodgedCount = () => results.filter((r) => r.outcome === 'dodged').length

  function paintStrip() {
    shell.setScore(String(dodgedCount()))
    shell.setMoves(String(results.length - dodgedCount()))
    shell.setLevel(`${Math.max(0, idx + 1)} / ${TOTAL}`)
  }

  function paintTally() {
    tally.forEach((li, k) => {
      const r = results[k]
      li.className = r ? (r.outcome === 'dodged' ? 'is-dodged' : 'is-fell') : k === idx ? 'is-now' : ''
      li.dataset.sign = r ? (r.outcome === 'dodged' ? '✓' : '✗') : ''
      li.firstElementChild!.textContent = r
        ? `Site ${k + 1}: ${r.outcome === 'dodged' ? 'dodged' : 'fell for it'}`
        : k === idx ? `Site ${k + 1}: now` : `Site ${k + 1}: not yet`
    })
  }

  const api: Api = {
    resolve(outcome, note) {
      if (resolved) return
      resolved = true
      clearTimers()
      slot.inert = true
      const p = PATTERNS[idx]
      results.push({ id: p.id, title: p.title, real: p.real, outcome, note })
      const good = outcome === 'dodged'
      verdict.className = 'dp-verdict ' + (good ? 'is-dodged' : 'is-fell')
      $('vSign').textContent = good ? '✓' : '✗'
      $('vHead').textContent = good ? 'You spotted it' : 'You fell for it'
      $('vTitle').textContent = p.title
      $('vNote').textContent = note
      $('vReveal').textContent = p.reveal
      $('vCite').textContent = `Catalogued in ${p.real}`
      $('nextLbl').textContent = idx + 1 >= TOTAL ? 'See how you did' : 'Next site'
      verdict.hidden = false
      if (good) { sfx.good(); shell.pop(verdict) }
      else { sfx.bad(); shell.shake(win) }
      shell.announce(`${good ? 'You spotted it' : 'You fell for it'}: ${p.title}.`)
      paintStrip()
      paintTally()
      verdict.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' })
      ;($('next') as HTMLButtonElement).focus({ preventScroll: true })
    },
    every(fn, ms) {
      timers.push(window.setInterval(() => { if (!shell.paused && !resolved) fn() }, ms))
    },
    knock() {
      site.classList.remove('is-knock')
      void site.offsetWidth
      site.classList.add('is-knock')
    },
  }

  function show(i: number) {
    clearTimers()
    if (i >= TOTAL) return finish()
    idx = i
    resolved = false
    const p = PATTERNS[i]
    const brand = BRANDS[p.id]
    win.dataset.brand = brand.block
    win.dataset.voice = brand.voice
    $('url').textContent = p.site
    $('favicon').textContent = brand.name.replace(/^the /i, '')[0].toUpperCase()
    $('wordmark').textContent = brand.name
    $('siteNo').textContent = `Site ${i + 1} of ${TOTAL}`
    $('lede').textContent = p.lede
    verdict.hidden = true
    slot.inert = false
    slot.innerHTML = ''
    // A new site: the load bar runs and the page wipes in from the top — the
    // small tell that this is a different place loading, not a relabel.
    for (const el of [$('load'), site]) {
      el.classList.remove('is-loading')
      void (el as HTMLElement).offsetWidth
      el.classList.add('is-loading')
    }
    MOUNTS[p.id](slot, api)
    shell.announce(`Site ${i + 1}: ${p.site}. ${p.lede}`)
    paintStrip()
    paintTally()
    if (i === TOTAL - 1) shell.levelUp('Last one.')
    site.focus({ preventScroll: true })
  }

  function begin() {
    unlock()
    sfx.click()
    intro.hidden = true
    play.hidden = false
    show(0)
    shell.stage.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' })
  }

  function restart() {
    clearTimers()
    results = []
    paintTally()
    begin()
  }

  $('begin').addEventListener('click', begin)
  $('next').addEventListener('click', () => { sfx.click(); show(idx + 1) })

  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.altKey || shell.paused) return
    const t = e.target as HTMLElement
    if (t.closest('input, textarea, select, dialog')) return
    const k = e.key.toLowerCase()
    if (!verdict.hidden && !play.hidden && (k === 'n' || (k === 'enter' && !t.closest('button, a')))) {
      e.preventDefault()
      show(idx + 1)
    } else if (!intro.hidden && k === 'enter' && !t.closest('button, a')) {
      e.preventDefault()
      begin()
    }
  })

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* The verdict                                                             */
  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  function finish() {
    const dodged = dodgedCount()
    const fell = results.length - dodged
    shell.resultExtra.innerHTML = `
      <table class="dp-sheet">
        <caption class="label">Every site, and which way you went</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Pattern</th><th scope="col">You</th><th scope="col">Catalogued in</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>${results.map((r) => `
          <tr class="${r.outcome === 'dodged' ? 'is-dodged' : 'is-fell'}">
            <th scope="row">${r.title}</th>
            <td>${r.outcome === 'dodged' ? '✓ Dodged' : '✗ Fell for it'}</td>
            <td>${r.real}</td>
          </tr>`).join('')}</tbody>
      </table>`

    recordPlay('dark-patterns', { dodged, fell, total: results.length }, { dodged: 'high' })
    const beat = shell.considerBest(dodged, `${dodged} / ${TOTAL}`)
    const lines = [
      fell === 0
        ? 'Every single one — and the real versions are built by people paid to make that hard.'
        : `You fell for ${fell}. Those are exactly the ones worth re-reading below: the mechanism is named next to each.`,
    ]
    if (beat === 'beaten') lines.push('✓ That is a new personal best.')
    else if (beat === 'first') lines.push('Your first run — that is the number to beat now.')
    else if (shell.best) lines.push(`Your best run is still ${shell.best.text}.`)
    const now = new Date()
    if (dailyFor(now).slug === 'dark-patterns') {
      const need = dailyTarget.dodges(now)
      lines.push(dodged >= need ? `✓ Daily challenge beaten: ${need} or more dodged.` : `✗ Daily challenge: dodge ${need} or more.`)
    }
    const ending = { kicker: `Site ${TOTAL} of ${TOTAL} · the verdict`, score: `${dodged} / ${TOTAL}`, from: `0 / ${TOTAL}`, lines, againLabel: 'Run it again' }
    if (dodged === TOTAL) shell.win({ ...ending, title: 'You saw through every one.' })
    else if (dodged > fell) shell.win({ ...ending, title: 'You saw through most of them.' })
    else shell.lose({ ...ending, title: 'The internet got you.' })
  }
</script>

<style is:global>
  /* The sites are built by the script, so these rules are global on purpose:
     scoped styles never reach runtime-built nodes. Everything is prefixed. */

  /* ---- intro --------------------------------------------------------- */
  .dp-intro { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 18px; padding: clamp(8px, 3vw, 40px) 0; max-width: 820px; }
  .dp-intro-title { font-size: var(--fs-h2); line-height: 0.98; max-width: 16ch; }
  .dp-intro .lead { max-width: 52ch; }
  .dp-domains { list-style: none; margin: 10px 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .dp-domains .tag { color: var(--ink2); text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; }

  /* ---- layout -------------------------------------------------------- */
  .dp-play { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(280px, 360px); gap: clamp(16px, 2.6vw, 36px); align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .dp-play { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }

  /* ---- the browser window -------------------------------------------- */
  .dp-window {
    --brand: var(--lilac);
    --brand-ink: var(--ink);
    position: relative;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .dp-window[data-brand='cobalt'] { --brand: var(--cobalt); }
  .dp-window[data-brand='mint'] { --brand: var(--mint); }
  .dp-window[data-brand='sky'] { --brand: var(--sky); }
  .dp-window[data-brand='red'] { --brand: var(--red); }
  .dp-window[data-brand='lilac'] { --brand: var(--lilac); }
  .dp-window[data-brand='ink'] { --brand: var(--ink); --brand-ink: var(--ink-paper); }

  .dp-chrome { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 10px 14px; background: var(--paper2); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .dp-lights { display: flex; gap: 6px; }
  .dp-lights i { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: var(--card); }
  .dp-addr {
    flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
    height: 32px; padding: 0 14px; border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    background: var(--card); border: 1.5px solid var(--paper3);
  }
  .dp-favicon {
    flex: none; width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 6px; display: grid; place-items: center;
    background: var(--brand); color: var(--brand-ink); font: 800 10px/1 var(--sans); font-style: normal;
  }
  .dp-url { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink2); white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .dp-load { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px; margin-top: -1px; background: var(--brand); transform-origin: left center; transform: scaleX(0); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }

  .dp-site { outline: none; }
  .dp-brandbar {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px;
    padding: 16px clamp(16px, 3vw, 28px);
    background: var(--brand); color: var(--brand-ink);
  }
  .dp-wordmark { font: 800 22px/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .dp-window[data-voice='serif'] .dp-wordmark { font-family: var(--display); font-variation-settings: var(--display-axes); font-weight: 600; font-style: italic; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .dp-window[data-voice='shout'] .dp-wordmark { font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 19px; }
  .dp-window[data-voice='lower'] .dp-wordmark { font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.05em; font-size: 26px; }
  .dp-nav { display: flex; gap: 16px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .dp-nav { display: none; } }

  .dp-body { position: relative; padding: clamp(18px, 3vw, 30px) clamp(16px, 3vw, 28px) clamp(22px, 3.4vw, 34px); min-height: 300px; display: grid; align-content: start; gap: 12px; }
  .dp-kicker { font-size: var(--fs-label); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink3); }
  .dp-h { font-family: var(--display); font-variation-settings: var(--display-axes); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 30px); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.02em; max-width: 24ch; }
  .dp-small { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink2); }
  .dp-center { text-align: center; }

  /* The two voices every site shares: the loud trap, the quiet way out. */
  .dp-trap {
    justify-self: start;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 8px;
    min-height: 54px; padding: 0 26px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    background: var(--brand); color: var(--brand-ink);
